  <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap; " class="mb-0 text-dark"><p>How to delete an upload in your github</p></pre>
</div>

  <div class="bg-secondary">
 <div data-react-class="AthenaRequestAnswer" data-react-props="{&quot;request&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:626343,&quot;broadcast_channel&quot;:&quot;athena-request-626343&quot;,&quot;answer_as_markdown&quot;:&quot;\u003cp\u003eTo delete an uploaded file from your GitHub repository, you can follow these steps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGo to your GitHub repository.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFind the file you want to delete in the file list.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick on the file to open it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOn the file page, look for the \&quot;Delete\&quot; icon (it looks like a trash can) and click it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou will be taken to a page where you can confirm the deletion. \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAfter you confirm, you can also add a commit message to explain the deletion.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFinally, click the \&quot;Commit changes\&quot; button to finalize the deletion.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eHere's how you can do it using \u003ccode\u003egit\u003c/code\u003e commands in your command line:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cheader\u003e\u003cdiv\u003ebash\u003c/div\u003e \u003cdiv class=\&quot;d-flex\&quot;\u003e \u003ci class=\&quot;fas fa-copy\&quot;\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003cdiv class=\&quot;clipboard-with-label-confirmation\&quot; data-clipboard-target=\&quot;#code-626343-0\&quot;\u003eCopy code\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/header\u003e\u003ccode class=\&quot;bash\&quot; id=\&quot;code-626343-0\&quot;\u003e# Navigate to your repository\ncd path/to/your/repository\n\n# Remove the file\ngit rm path/to/your/file\n\n# Commit the change\ngit commit -m \&quot;Deleted the file\&quot;\n\n# Push the changes to GitHub\ngit push origin main\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eMake sure to replace \u003ccode\u003epath/to/your/file\u003c/code\u003e with the actual path of the file you want to delete. If you're using a different branch instead of \u003ccode\u003emain\u003c/code\u003e, replace it with your branch name. \u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor more detailed information, you can check the GitHub documentation: \u003ca href=\&quot;https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/working-with-files/deleting-files\&quot; target=\&quot;_blank\&quot;\u003eDeleting a file from your GitHub repository\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n&quot;,&quot;downvote_path&quot;:&quot;/athena_requests/626343/downvote&quot;,&quot;upvote_path&quot;:&quot;/athena_requests/626343/upvote&quot;,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;downvoted&quot;:false,&quot;parent_id&quot;:null,&quot;children&quot;:[],&quot;state&quot;:&quot;processed&quot;,&quot;answer&quot;:&quot;To delete an uploaded file from your GitHub repository, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Go to your GitHub repository.\n2. Find the file you want to delete in the file list.\n3. Click on the file to open it.\n4. On the file page, look for the \&quot;Delete\&quot; icon (it looks like a trash can) and click it.\n5. You will be taken to a page where you can confirm the deletion. \n6. After you confirm, you can also add a commit message to explain the deletion.\n7. Finally, click the \&quot;Commit changes\&quot; button to finalize the deletion.\n\nHere's how you can do it using `git` commands in your command line:\n\n```bash\n# Navigate to your repository\ncd path/to/your/repository\n\n# Remove the file\ngit rm path/to/your/file\n\n# Commit the change\ngit commit -m \&quot;Deleted the file\&quot;\n\n# Push the changes to GitHub\ngit push origin main\n```\n\nMake sure to replace `path/to/your/file` with the actual path of the file you want to delete. If you're using a different branch instead of `main`, replace it with your branch name. \n\nFor more detailed information, you can check the GitHub documentation: [Deleting a file from your GitHub repository](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/working-with-files/deleting-files).&quot;,&quot;question&quot;:&quot;How to delete an upload in your github &quot;,&quot;question_type&quot;:&quot;question&quot;,&quot;question_format&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;processing_time&quot;:4.35,&quot;root_question_type&quot;:&quot;question&quot;},&quot;hideStatus&quot;:true}" data-react-cache-id="AthenaRequestAnswer-0"><div><div class="athena-request athena-request-answer"><div class="d-flex justify-content-between"><h3>🤖 SheCodes Athena says:</h3><div class="d-flex"><div class="text-muted d-none d-lg-block">Answered in 4.35 seconds</div></div></div><div><p>To delete an uploaded file from your GitHub repository, you can follow these steps:</p>

<ol>
<li>Go to your GitHub repository.</li>
<li>Find the file you want to delete in the file list.</li>
<li>Click on the file to open it.</li>
<li>On the file page, look for the "Delete" icon (it looks like a trash can) and click it.</li>
<li>You will be taken to a page where you can confirm the deletion. </li>
<li>After you confirm, you can also add a commit message to explain the deletion.</li>
<li>Finally, click the "Commit changes" button to finalize the deletion.</li>
</ol>

<p>Here's how you can do it using <code>git</code> commands in your command line:</p>

<pre><header><div>bash</div> <div class="d-flex"> <i class="fas fa-copy" aria-hidden="true"></i><div class="clipboard-with-label-confirmation" data-clipboard-target="#code-626343-0">Copy code</div>
</div></header><code class="bash hljs language-bash" id="code-626343-0" data-highlighted="yes"><span class="hljs-comment"># Navigate to your repository</span>
<span class="hljs-built_in">cd</span> path/to/your/repository

<span class="hljs-comment"># Remove the file</span>
git <span class="hljs-built_in">rm</span> path/to/your/file

<span class="hljs-comment"># Commit the change</span>
git commit -m <span class="hljs-string">"Deleted the file"</span>

<span class="hljs-comment"># Push the changes to GitHub</span>
git push origin main
</code></pre>

<p>Make sure to replace <code>path/to/your/file</code> with the actual path of the file you want to delete. If you're using a different branch instead of <code>main</code>, replace it with your branch name. </p>

<p>For more detailed information, you can check the GitHub documentation: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/working-with-files/deleting-files" target="_blank">Deleting a file from your GitHub repository</a>.</p>
</div></div></div></div>
