  <div class="bg-secondary">
 <div data-react-class="AthenaRequestAnswer" data-react-props="{&quot;request&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:625468,&quot;broadcast_channel&quot;:&quot;athena-request-625468&quot;,&quot;answer_as_markdown&quot;:&quot;\u003cp\u003eYou can loop through the properties of an object in JavaScript using a \u003ccode\u003efor...in\u003c/code\u003e loop or \u003ccode\u003eObject.keys()\u003c/code\u003e method. Here are examples of both:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eUsing \u003ccode\u003efor...in\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cheader\u003e\u003cdiv\u003ejavascript\u003c/div\u003e \u003cdiv class=\&quot;d-flex\&quot;\u003e \u003ci class=\&quot;fas fa-copy\&quot;\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003cdiv class=\&quot;clipboard-with-label-confirmation\&quot; data-clipboard-target=\&quot;#code-625468-0\&quot;\u003eCopy code\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/header\u003e\u003ccode class=\&quot;javascript\&quot; id=\&quot;code-625468-0\&quot;\u003econst obj = { a: 1, b: 2, c: 3 };\n\nfor (let key in obj) {\n  console.log(key, obj[key]);\n}\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eUsing \u003ccode\u003eObject.keys()\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cheader\u003e\u003cdiv\u003ejavascript\u003c/div\u003e \u003cdiv class=\&quot;d-flex\&quot;\u003e \u003ci class=\&quot;fas fa-copy\&quot;\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003cdiv class=\&quot;clipboard-with-label-confirmation\&quot; data-clipboard-target=\&quot;#code-625468-1\&quot;\u003eCopy code\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/header\u003e\u003ccode class=\&quot;javascript\&quot; id=\&quot;code-625468-1\&quot;\u003econst obj = { a: 1, b: 2, c: 3 };\n\nObject.keys(obj).forEach(key =\u0026gt; {\n  console.log(key, obj[key]);\n});\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eBoth methods will loop through the keys of the object and allow you to access their values.\u003c/p\u003e\n&quot;,&quot;downvote_path&quot;:&quot;/athena_requests/625468/downvote&quot;,&quot;upvote_path&quot;:&quot;/athena_r