 <div data-react-class="AthenaRequestAnswer" data-react-props="{&quot;request&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:607950,&quot;broadcast_channel&quot;:&quot;athena-request-607950&quot;,&quot;answer_as_markdown&quot;:&quot;\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eparseFloat\u003c/code\u003e is a built-in JavaScript function that converts a string into a floating-point number (a number that can have decimals). It's useful when you want to take a string that represents a number and turn it into a format that you can perform calculations with.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eHere's how it works:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cheader\u003e\u003cdiv\u003ejavascript\u003c/div\u003e \u003cdiv class=\&quot;d-flex\&quot;\u003e \u003ci class=\&quot;fas fa-copy\&quot;\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003cdiv class=\&quot;clipboard-with-label-confirmation\&quot; data-clipboard-target=\&quot;#code-607950-0\&quot;\u003eCopy code\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/header\u003e\u003ccode class=\&quot;javascript\&quot; id=\&quot;code-607950-0\&quot;\u003elet stringNumber = \&quot;3.14\&quot;;\nlet floatNumber = parseFloat(stringNumber);\n\nconsole.log(floatNumber); // Outputs: 3.14\nconsole.log(typeof floatNumber); // Outputs: \&quot;number\&quot;\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIn this example, \u003ccode\u003eparseFloat\u003c/code\u003e takes the string \u003ccode\u003e\&quot;3.14\&quot;\u003c/code\u003e and converts it to the number \u003ccode\u003e3.14\u003c/code\u003e. If the string doesn't start with a number, it will return \u003ccode\u003eNaN\u003c/code\u003e (which means \&quot;Not-a-Number\&quot;). \u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, you can check the \u003ca href=\&quot;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/parseFloat\&quot; target=\&quot;_blank\&quot;\u003eMDN documentation on parseFloat\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n&quot;,&quot;downvote_path&quot;:&quot;/athena_requests/607950/downvote&quot;,&quot;upvote_path&quot;:&quot;/athena_requests/607950/upvote&quot;,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;downvoted&quot;:false,&quot;parent_id&quot;:null,&quot;children&quot;:[],&quot;state&quot;:&quot;processed&quot;,&quot;answer&quot;:&quot;`parseFloat` is a built-in JavaScript function that converts a string into a floating-point number (a number that can have decimals). It's useful when you want to take a string that represents a number and turn it into a format that you can perform calculations with.\n\nHere's how it works:\n\n```javascript\nlet stringNumber = \&quot;3.14\&quot;;\nlet floatNumber = parseFloat(stringNumber);\n\nconsole.log(floatNumber); // Outputs: 3.14\nconsole.log(typeof floatNumber); // Outputs: \&quot;number\&quot;\n```\n\nIn this example, `parseFloat` takes the string `\&quot;3.14\&quot;` and converts it to the number `3.14`. If the string doesn't start with a number, it will return `NaN` (which means \&quot;Not-a-Number\&quot;). \n\nFor more information, you can check the [MDN documentation on parseFloat](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/parseFloat).&quot;,&quot;question&quot;:&quot;What does parse float mean in JavaScript &quot;,&quot;question_type&quot;:&quot;question&quot;,&quot;question_format&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;processing_time&quot;:2.73,&quot;root_question_type&quot;:&quot;question&quot;},&quot;hideStatus&quot;:true}" data-react-cache-id="AthenaRequestAnswer-0"><div><div class="athena-request athena-request-answer"><div class="d-flex justify-content-between"><h3>🤖 SheCodes Athena says:</h3><div class="d-flex"><div class="text-muted d-none d-lg-block">Answered in 2.73 seconds</div></div></div><div><p><code>parseFloat</code> is a built-in JavaScript function that converts a string into a floating-point number (a number that can have decimals). It's useful when you want to take a string that represents a number and turn it into a format that you can perform calculations with.</p>

<p>Here's how it works:</p>

<pre><header><div>javascript</div> <div class="d-flex"> <i class="fas fa-copy" aria-hidden="true"></i><div class="clipboard-with-label-confirmation" data-clipboard-target="#code-607950-0">Copy code</div>
</div></header><code class="javascript hljs language-javascript" id="code-607950-0" data-highlighted="yes"><span class="hljs-keyword">let</span> stringNumber = <span class="hljs-string">"3.14"</span>;
