  <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap; " class="mb-0 text-dark"><p>What is const</p></pre>
</div>

  <div class="bg-secondary">
 <div data-react-class="AthenaRequestAnswer" data-react-props="{&quot;request&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:576389,&quot;broadcast_channel&quot;:&quot;athena-request-576389&quot;,&quot;answer_as_markdown&quot;:&quot;\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003econst\u003c/code\u003e is a keyword in JavaScript that is used to declare a variable whose value cannot be changed (or reassigned) after it is defined. It stands for \&quot;constant\&quot;. This means that once you set a value to a variable using \u003ccode\u003econst\u003c/code\u003e, you cannot change that value later in the code.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eHere's a simple example:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003cheader\u003e\u003cdiv\u003ejavascript\u003c/div\u003e \u003cdiv class=\&quot;d-flex\&quot;\u003e \u003ci class=\&quot;fas fa-copy\&quot;\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003cdiv class=\&quot;clipboard-with-label-confirmation\&quot; data-clipboard-target=\&quot;#code-576389-0\&quot;\u003eCopy code\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/header\u003e\u003ccode class=\&quot;javascript\&quot; id=\&quot;code-576389-0\&quot;\u003econst pi = 3.14;\nconsole.log(pi); // Outputs: 3.14\n\n// This line would cause an error because you cannot reassign a constant variable\n// pi = 3.14159; // Uncaught TypeError: Assignment to constant variable.\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, you can check the \u003ca href=\&quot;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/const\&quot; target=\&quot;_blank\&quot;\u003eMDN Web Docs on const\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n&quot;,&quot;downvote_path&quot;:&quot;/athena_requests/576389/downvote&quot;,&quot;upvote_path&quot;:&quot;/athena_requests/576389/upvote&quot;,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;downvoted&quot;:false,&quot;parent_id&quot;:null,&quot;children&quot;:[],&quot;state&quot;:&quot;processed&quot;,&quot;answer&quot;:&quot;`const` is a keyword in JavaScript that is used to declare a variable whose value cannot be changed (or reassigned) after it is defined. It stands for \&quot;constant\&quot;. This means that once you set a value to a variable using `const`, you cannot change that value later in the code.\n\nHere's a simple example:\n\n```javascript\nconst pi = 3.14;\nconsole.log(pi); // Outputs: 3.14\n\n// This line would cause an error because you cannot reassign a constant variable\n// pi = 3.14159; // Uncaught TypeError: Assignment to constant variable.\n```\n\nFor more information, you can check the [MDN Web Docs on const](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/const).&quot;,&quot;question&quot;:&quot;What is const\r\n&quot;,&quot;question_type&quot;:&quot;question&quot;,&quot;question_format&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;processing_time&quot;:2.25,&quot;root_question_type&quot;:&quot;question&quot;},&quot;hideStatus&quot;:true}" data-react-cache-id="AthenaRequestAnswer-0"><div><div class="athena-request athena-request-answer"><div class="d-flex justify-content-between"><h3>🤖 SheCodes Athena says:</h3><div class="d-flex"><div class="text-muted d-none d-lg-block">Answered in 2.25 seconds</div></div></div><div><p><code>const</code> is a keyword in JavaScript that is used to declare a variable whose value cannot be changed (or reassigned) after it is defined. It stands for "constant". This means that once you set a value to a variable using <code>const</code>, you cannot change that value later in the code.</p>

<p>Here's a simple example:</p>

<pre><header><div>javascript</div> <div class="d-flex"> <i class="fas fa-copy" aria-hidden="true"></i><div class="clipboard-with-label-confirmation" data-clipboard-target="#code-576389-0">Copy code</div>
</div></header><code class="javascript hljs language-javascript" id="code-576389-0" data-highlighted="yes"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> pi = <span class="hljs-number">3.14</span>;
<span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">log</span>(pi); <span class="hljs-comment">// Outputs: 3.14</span>

<span class="hljs-comment">// This line would cause an error because you cannot reassign a constant variable</span>
<span class="hljs-comment">// pi = 3.14159; // Uncaught TypeError: Assignment to constant variable.</span>
</code></pre>

<p>For more information, you can check the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/const" target="_blank">MDN Web Docs on const</a>.</p>
</div></div></div></div>
</div>
